BOM Compare Excel Download Template 
 
The BomCompare.vm velocity template is an example for downloading a BOM Comparison into 
excel.  

The template has the follwing variables defined in its context 

	1. $ISO8601 - The ISO8601 class useful to format dates as text by 
				  calling the safeFormat function 
	2. $STRESC - Utility class to csv escape text data (org.apache.commons.lang.StringEscapeUtils)
	3. $date - The DateTool class http://velocity.apache.org/tools/devel/javadoc/org/apache/velocity/tools/generic/DateTool.html
	4. $CONFIG - The ConfigurationUtils class to access configuration information
	5. $MCMMessages - The MCMMessages class to access properties in the scplatform-messages.properties file
	5. $form - The form containing the BOM comparison results 
	 
In order to successfully download the BOM Comparison, the excel workbook must 
have a template sheet called "BomCompare" (no quotes). This sheet will require two 
header rows. The first row contains the BOM information about the BOMs being compared
and the second row contains the attributes of each BOM Line based on the compare criteria
in the Compare.xml BOM Comparison configuration file.  The actual data is populated from row three.
The BOM Comparison excel file cannot be uploaded.  It is for information purposes only. 

$form
===========
The $form variable is the object that provides access to the list of comparison criteria as well as the BOM Comparison results.
This is the same object that is used to display the BOM Comparison results in the UI.

The following form methods are used:
 * $form.compareCriteria - The attributes defined in the compareCriteria list in the Compare.xml
 	BOM Comparison configuration file
 * $form.compareResult - The object that contains the BOM Comparison results.  It is assigned to
 	the result variable.
 	* $result.leftBom - The BOM that is on the left side of the comparison.
 	* $result.rightBom - The BOM that is on the right side of the comparison.
 	* $result.lineResults - The comparison results for each BOM Line.  It is assigned to
 	   the line variable.
 	   * $line.leftPropValues - A Map that contains the values for each criteria attribute.  The map key
 	      is the criteria attribute and the value is the value of the attribute from the specified BOM Line
 	      in the Left BOM.
 	   * $line.rightPropValues - A Map that contains the values for each criteria attribute.  The map key
 	      is the criteria attribute and the value is the value of the attribute from the specified BOM Line
 	      in the Right BOM.
 	   * $line.level - the level of the line within the BOM
 	   * $line.left.item.itemNumber - the item identifier of the the Left BOM Line
 	   * $line.operation - the operation that is being performed between the Left BOM Line and the
 	      Right BOM Line.
 	   * $line.right.item.itemNumber - the item identifier of the the Right BOM Line

